# Tracer: native mathematical constants
#
# Before (Litex verified, but compiler emission stopped):
# pi $in R
# Former compiler behavior: IR capture stopped at line 16 because the generic
# `native mathematical constant is a real` label had no To-Lean proof rule.
#
# Now: `i`, `e`, and `pi` lower to native Mathlib complex terms. Base-carrier
# memberships replay exact verifier-selected certificates through proved rules.
i = i
e = e
pi = pi

i $in C
e $in R
pi $in R
e $in C
pi $in C

# Handoff (implemented by Example 21):
# e $in R+
# Positive-real membership uses its own exact refined carrier and must not
# erase that predicate or reuse plain `R`.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -graph -f lean/examples/19_NativeConstants.lit
# cargo test --release --test stmt_result_to_lean_compiler_tracers native_constants
# cd lean && ./stmt_result_to_lean_compiler.sh check examples
